    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Discover your dream coastal retreat at 33 Dún Árd, Doon Road, Ballybunion, an exceptional property perfectly positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac within this world-famous seaside resort.  This beautifully presented, timber-framed, two-storey end-of-terrace home extends to approximately 105 sq.m of bright, light-filled, and spacious accommodation. The ground floor layout comprises an inviting sitting room, an open-plan kitchen and dining area, a practical utility room, and a convenient guest shower room, while upstairs features three generous bedrooms (including one en-suite) and a modern family shower room.\r\n\r\nStep outside to appreciate the stunning, uniquely scenic surroundings; the property overlooks a peaceful, designated green area to the front, while the south-facing rear aspect commands breathtaking, panoramic views of the Atlantic Ocean, Ballybunion town, the Cashen River, and the rolling Irish countryside. Ideal for families and outdoor enthusiasts alike, the home features ample car parking and a secure, enclosed rear garden complete with a solid block-built wall and handy garden shed.\r\n\r\nLocation is everything, and No. 33 places you within comfortable walking distance of both local primary and secondary schools, vibrant shops, pristine beaches, and essential amenities, while the world-renowned Ballybunion Golf Club is just a short drive away. With all public services connected, efficient oil-fired central heating, and an excellent B3 BER rating qualifying you for competitive Green Energy Mortgage rates, this property represents an unrivaled opportunity for a family home, holiday escape, or investment. Call 068 21739 today to arrange your private viewing."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 5.6m x 2.0m \r\nTiled flooring, newly fitted front door, gable window looking onto manicured lawn and planted area - staircase to first floor with fitted carpet.\r\n\r\nSitting room - 4.2m x 4.2m \r\nPolished oak flooring, marble fireplace with solid fuel stove insert and feature bay window overlooking the designated green area.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining - 4.8m x 3.7m \r\nTiled flooring, fully fitted kitchen wood, with integrated fridge freezer, electric oven, ceramic hob, extractor fan, integrated dishwasher, stainless steel sink, recessed ceiling light and large window overlooking the manicure South facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nUtility Room - 2.0m x 2.2m \r\nTiled flooring,  plumbed for washing and drying appliances (not included) - rear door access to rear garden.\r\n\r\nShower Room - 2.0m x 1.4m \r\nFully tiled floor to ceiling, Triton Power shower, frosted window, toilet and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.5m x 2.0m \r\nGable window, fitted hot-press and Stira access to attic.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.0m x 2.8m \r\nWith tongue and grooved French pine flooring - overlooking the rear garden.  Capturing views of the Atlantic Ocean, Kerry Head,  Mount Brandon, The Cashen river and surrounding countryside.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 2.9m x 3.5m \r\nWith tongue and grooved French pine flooring - walk-in wardrobe space (1.0m x 1.4m) - overlooking the rear garden.  Capturing views of the Atlantic Ocean, Kerry Head,  Mount Brandon, The Cashen river and surrounding countryside.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.5m x 3.0m \r\nWith tongue and grooved French pine flooring, recessed space for built-in wardrobes and two windows overlooking the designated green area.  Ensuite, fully tiled floor to ceiling with electric shower, toilet, wash hand basin and mechanical vent.\r\n\r\nFamily Shower Room - 2.0m x 2.8m \r\nFully tiled floor to ceiling complete with large walk-in Power shower, toilet, wash hand basin and frosted window.\r\n\r\nTimber Garden Shed - 2.0m x 2.0m \r\n\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "B3 Green Energy mortgage rates.\r\nEnd of terrace two storey timber frame built House 2007.\r\nOil fired central heating with wall mounted radiators.\r\nComplete with smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarm.\r\nWired for intruder alarm system and broadband.\r\nDouble glazed PVC doors and windows throughout.\r\nBlock built boundary walls with secure pedestrian side access. \r\nManicured gardens and set down paved patio area.\r\nSouth facing aspect and car parking in front of house."
      },
